From fe11030d4f75b6704817b6972a15d99b7c5e0a8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:13:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pf proxier: serialize pfctl loads and retry when pf is busy

On a dual-stack node kube-proxy runs one pf proxier per IP family and
both sync at the same time. Loading an anchor takes a ticket for pf's
address pool buffer, of which there is one for the whole system, so
concurrent loads invalidated each other: 'DIOCADDADDR: Device busy' /
'DIOCADDRULE: Device busy', hundreds per hour, and the Service whose
anchor failed kept stale rules (or none), because the failure was only
logged.

Run every pfctl command that changes pf through runPfctl: one at a time
per process, retried a few times while pf reports the device busy
(bsd-netpol and the CNI portmap plugin also load rules). When an anchor
still fails to load, syncProxyRules returns an error so the runner
retries the sync.
---
 pkg/proxy/pf/pfctl.go      |  61 +++++++++++++++++++++
 pkg/proxy/pf/pfctl_test.go | 106 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 pkg/proxy/pf/proxier.go    |  15 +++---
 pkg/proxy/pf/udpstates.go  |   2 +-
 4 files changed, 177 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 pkg/proxy/pf/pfctl.go
 create mode 100644 pkg/proxy/pf/pfctl_test.go

diff --git a/pkg/proxy/pf/pfctl.go b/pkg/proxy/pf/pfctl.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..1f98d074a10
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pkg/proxy/pf/pfctl.go
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
